  id: poi-b
  title: "Eleventh-Bell Collectors"
  situation: "After the eleventh bell Draught Lane empties faster than it should. A side-coach without crest lamps waits past the coal stairs. Two figures in coach-coats drag a screaming mill girl toward the alley; another girl fights free for one breath. A distant Warden whistle is too far. (11.1 POI B)"
  poi: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5bbaf1dc5f44490bb3d32f8359246335, type: 2}
  scene: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3f5b7d9e1a2c4e5f7a9b1c3d5e7f9a2b, type: 2}
  primaryAxis: 2
  secondaryAxis: 1
  options:
  - name: "Protect the victims now"
    axes:
    - 2
    - 1
    approaches:
    - 5
    - 1
    - 2
    dialogueOptions:
    - swarm
    - threaten
    cost: "A threat on the collectors is a Final Check: a failure is a fight, which before S3 ends the scene as if fled (the lane's Veinmarket outcome)"
    consequence: "The girls free tonight"
    opens: "Gratitude, and the girl's word that the collectors asked who bought black cough from Harrow"
    closes: "A clean trail to the destination; Veinmarket's goodwill, as the collectors are its men (11)"
    failure: "Roused doors stay shut; a failed threat loses the girls"
    residue:
    - aftermath.loom_lane.girls_freed
    - against.veinmarket
    - poi.b.heard.harrow_buyers
